  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says that in the 1960s a man named Lewis Branscomb, a protégé of the scientist Donald Menzel, gave the physicist Edward Condon back his security clearance. Michels says Condon then did a \"hit job\" on UFOs through the Condon Committee, a study of UFOs he led, and that this ended Blue Book, the US Air Force's UFO study of the 1950s and 60s. If true, it would mean the study that closed the official UFO investigation was steered from the start."
